    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nFor constant angular deceleration to rest, the average angular speed is $\\omega_{\\text{avg}} = \\frac{\\omega_0}{2}$. The total revolutions is $N = \\frac{n_0}{2} t$.\n\n2. GIVEN:\nInitial frequency n0 = 70 rps, final frequency 0, time t = 15 s.\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\nN = \\frac{n_0}{2} t\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. Average rotational speed: n_avg = 70 / 2 = 35.0 rev/s.\n2. Total revolutions made: N = n_avg * t = 35.0 * 15 = 525.0 revolutions.\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption A: 525.0 revolutions\n\n6. QUICK TIP:\nDirect shortcut: for uniform deceleration to rest, total revolutions = (initial frequency / 2) * time!",
